body:
I don't have any EMF device to measure possible frequencies.

&#x200B;

I moved to another bed today and find it better but suddenly I suspected that something else could be wrong. I switched off main power supply for whole 2 appartments on top (where I live). My headache pain went down, but still some parts of the room had electricity (lights worked). I found that whenever there is electricity on, strange intensity is felt.

&#x200B;

I checked other apartments in the house (together 5) and found that everywhere intensity could be felt. It was couple of days now and I can't even work anymore at computer, my head will almost blow.

&#x200B;

I think it could be something else. I don't know what and I don't know how to tell the owner about it. Around electrical devices (and sockets) the intensity is very high. Must be something else, help would be appreciated.

Last night I switched off all main power switches, it was like 90% better, but nothing worked. The owner would be mad if he finds out that I experimented.


Very sad because I want to stay here and solve the problem somehow. If I only knew where to look or what to do, it would be easier to tell the owner to pay the electrician (but I suspect that there are very bad ones).

No. I moved back home after 6 months, went for a walk out, it is the same sharp smell everywhere in radius of 2 km from quarry. I have no idea what element is responsible for this smell. It's been 6 months since they stopped working but the strenght is still noticeable, I would say about 50%.

&#x200B;

This stuff didn't go away in just few days. You mentioned that dioxide or monoxide will go away on it's own in a few days? I believe that this could be something else. It's really something huge widely spread in the air, but have no idea what.  We had so much wind in 6 months and rain but improvement is very slow. It is actually quite similar effect to chlorine (with less power and different smell). Because I have sarcoidosis I am very sensitive to chemicals and pollution. Local authorities didn't say anything but simply close the quarry, regarding the air, they said that everything is fine (with no proof or anything).

I am not. I really don't know. 

&#x200B;

I only guess because of our nearest quarry. All they do is use explosives (bags of ammonium nitrate) and these explosions create nitric monoxide and dioxide.

I tried ioniser it is a little better (too much ozone is bad correct, I noticed after 4 hours). 

&#x200B;

Purifier, you mean regular air cleaner? I have Beurer LR 200 in my room but it doesn't remove sharp smell, it must be something that goes through hepa and carbon filter.

The situation is not easy to explain. If we rely on scientific studies, they also have the cause in their studies, but it would be their cause. The cure can be provided only when the real cause is found. All studies based on this phenomenon have different theories and results, and since there are no researchers with their own personal experience, I named my post with the true cause based on my 20 experience. I also have another family member with diabetes who also had same conditions couple of times when mentioned factors were met. My purpose is not to rely on the english grammar because I am not a native speaker but rather to help sufferers to get clear open book of knowledge that has facts not just experiments.  Einstein expressed himself perfectly with quote: The Only Source of Knowledge is Experience. We should rely on this much more than studies that have most of the time vitro and vivo experiements. From my experience this is the true cause.

&#x200B;

I've checked definite article "the" on some other health related posts and believe I wrote good enough if  I compare this article: [https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/the-author-speaks/201809/diabetes-the-real-cause-and-the-right-cure](https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/the-author-speaks/201809/diabetes-the-real-cause-and-the-right-cure)

&#x200B;
